        <body>
            <div xml:id="d545">

                <pb facs="1015" n="891" sameAs="frus:frus1881/pg891"/>

                <head>No. 541.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Christiancy to Mr.
                    Blaine.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Lima, Peru</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1881-04-04"><hi rendition="#italic">April</hi> 4, 1881</date>.
                        (Received April 26.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 276.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to my dispatch No. 256 (second
                    paragraph), in which I stated, in substance, upon report, among other things,
                    that the Chilians had taken from the exposition grounds, belonging to the
                    Benevolent Society of Lima, the collection of animals there, I have now to make
                    this correction, viz: That these animals had not <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >then</hi> been taken (a few days since), but preparations had been made to
                    take them, and the cages were already taken to the grounds, in which they were
                    to be shipped, and there is no doubt they will be taken.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>I. P. CHRISTIANCY.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
